{
 "_doc": {
  "what": "GOLD-HEADBAND -- hand-assigned region labels for every readable token in the top 3 rows of OT1-1609-B leaves 400-419. The reference set for R2.1g / R2.2a's RunningHead/MainText separator.",
  "why_tracked": "R11 rule (OCR-MASTERPLAN 0.2 rule 6): evidence that lives in gitignored .scratch is checkable on one machine only. The probes that produced the geometry are scratch; the LABELS are the deliverable and are tracked.",
  "labelling_basis": "LABELS COME FROM WHAT THE TOKEN SAYS, NEVER FROM WHERE IT SITS. The separator under test uses position, justification and glyph density; labelling by position would score the instrument against its own signal and guarantee a pass. 'NVMERI' is the book's name and is a running head wherever it appears. Scripture is main text. 'Vowes.', 'Madianites', 'Fornicat', 'al festiuities', 'Daughters may inherite.' are the printed side-notes of this edition. This is the vocabulary of the BOOK, not of the error (Sir's anti-circularity ruling, 2026-08-17).",
  "labels": {
   "RH": "running head -- the book name set across the head of the page",
   "MN": "marginal note -- the printed side-note, set in the outer margin",
   "MT": "main text -- scripture in the text block",
   "CH": "chapter head -- CHAP. + numeral"
  },
  "excluded": "Tokens carrying fewer than 3 glyph components, and tokens the recogniser returned empty for, are NOT labelled and are NOT scored. They are counted and reported as `unlabelled` by the scorer -- never silently dropped (R1.4). Four further tokens are excluded as GENUINELY AMBIGUOUS and are listed in `ambiguous` with the reason; excluding them is recorded rather than hidden because an ambiguous token silently labelled is a gold-set defect.",
  "source_probe": ".scratch/r2/dump_headtokens.py -> .scratch/r2/headtokens.json",
  "witness": "OT1-1609-B",
  "window": "leaves 400-419 -- THE SAME WINDOW R2.1d'(A) scored 0.312 on, so the numbers are directly comparable",
  "dated": "2026-08-17",
  "addressing": "⚠️ v2, R2.1i. A label is addressed by its BAND-PIXEL SPAN (l, r) within a row, NOT by a token ordinal. v1 used the ordinal, and because the ordinal is an index into a list whose length depends on the splitter, changing the splitter renumbered every key and collapsed the score with no region having changed (MN recall 0.8947 -> 0.5263, unlabelled 80 -> 212). An instrument that reads a tokenisation improvement as a region regression punishes progress. Scoring matches each label to the token of maximal span overlap. ⚠️ ADDRESSING IS NOT ADJUDICATION: geometry says WHICH token a label belongs to; it never says WHAT the label is -- the labels remain the ones read off the text in v1, unchanged.",
  "band": "0.0..0.35 of page height, resized to width 1400. Spans are in THAT band's pixels.",
  "v2_dated": "2026-08-17",
  "ambiguous_addressing": "v2, R2.1i: the ambiguous list is addressed by span too. Left on ordinals it would have drifted independently of the labels, which is a worse failure than the one being fixed -- an exclusion silently pointing at the wrong token re-admits the token it was written to exclude.",
  "address": "TWO ADDRESSES, both live, and a consumer must choose deliberately. (a) `row`,`l`,`r` are BAND PIXELS in the 0..0.35h crop at width 1400 -- the address every recorded number (0.8760 max-overlap, the R2.1j ink figures) was measured against, kept so those stay reproducible. ⚠️ `row` is an ORDINAL into a list THE BAND CONTROLS, so this address is only meaningful to a consumer cropping 0..0.35h. (b) `xlf`,`xrf`,`y0f`,`y1f` are fractions of PAGE width/height -- band-independent, and the address R2.2c added because the production reader crops 0.06h..0.30h, in which 0 of 20 RunningHead entries and 2 of 19 MarginNote entries lie. Prefer (b) for any question about WHERE ON THE PAGE a label is; (a) is for reproducing the recorded scores. Written by witness/gold_rekey_pagefrac.py."
 },
